WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.900 line:10% align:center
[Low strings enter]

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.325 line:10% align:center
An agreement is more than words.

00:00:03.665 --> 00:00:06.865 line:10% align:center
What happens when the code disagrees
with the promise?

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.067 line:10% align:center
Meet LegalX.

00:00:11.407 --> 00:00:16.441 line:10% align:center
Design, build, and delivery.
Three approvals release three equal payments.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.311 line:10% align:center
Here, a separate website agreement
shows how intake works.

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:26.426 line:10% align:center
Local extraction links each payment
to its source clause.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.535 line:10% align:center
Contract IR gives the agreement a structure.

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:35.432 line:10% align:center
Inspect the milestones, the review window,
and the evidence behind each field.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.640 line:10% align:center
[Two descending tones]

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.947 line:10% align:center
₹30,000 agreed. ₹35,000 encoded.

00:00:41.287 --> 00:00:43.783 line:10% align:center
A ₹5,000 discrepancy.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.462 line:10% align:center
Watch the review period change.
Verification catches the mismatch.

00:00:49.802 --> 00:00:53.431 line:10% align:center
Restoring the terms still leaves
human approval as a separate gate.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:54.640 line:10% align:center
[Closing chime]

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.789 line:10% align:center
LegalX.

00:00:56.409 --> 00:01:01.465 line:10% align:center
Verify the agreement. Review the evidence.
Then decide whether to execute.

